ame><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKUDA HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMIYAMA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEYAMA MASASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEYAMA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKIYAMA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOSHIO, SHUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANABE, SHOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKUDA, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMIYAMA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEYAMA, MASASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEYAMA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A synthetic resin thin wall container, wherein a shell part comprises front and rear walls and side walls, the front and rear walls are formed in an elliptic shape in lateral cross-section and recessed grooves extending in lateral direction are disposed therein; the side walls are formed in vertical flat planes which cuts off the both ends of the elliptic shape of the front and rear walls, and a plurality of reinforced parts are disposed on the surface thereof; the bottom part comprises a bottom peripheral wall continuing from the shell part and a bottom wall, the bottom peripheral wall is formed of slightly inclined front and rear walls and right and left side walls inclined at a specified angle, and reinforcing ribs are disposed on the bottom peripheral wall.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un contenant à parois minces en résine synthétique, dans lequel une partie d'enveloppe comporte des parois antérieure et postérieure ainsi que des parois latérales, les parois antérieure et postérieure présentent une forme elliptique en section latérale et contiennent des rainures creuses s'étendant dans le sens latéral ; les parois latérales sont formées en plans plats verticaux qui coupent les deux extrémités de la forme elliptique des parois antérieure et postérieure, et comportent sur leur surface plusieurs parties renforcées; la partie inférieure comporte une paroi périphérique inférieure continuant la partie d'enveloppe et une paroi inférieure, cette paroi périphérique inférieure étant formée de parois antérieure et postérieure légèrement inclinées et de parois latérales gauche et droite inclinées selon un angle spécifique, et comportant des nervures de renforcement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>